WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.150
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.150
Brother...

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.650
Get out of your TSF and surrender.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.860
Otherwise, I can't guarantee her safety.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:20.360
The Western Theatre forces' command 
center will soon be captured.

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.160
It's all over.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.480
Please get out.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.880
I won't hurt either of you.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.390
L-Lise...

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:32.670
What's this?

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.080
Unidentified TSFs approaching 
from the northwest?

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.290
Theodor!

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.680
Run, Theodor!

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.730
Shut up!

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.890
If it weren't...

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.900
If it weren't for you...

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:48.950
Go...

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.650
Go, Theodor!

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.310
Go and get a future for us!

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.940
Damn it! Damn it!

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.170
Damn it!

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:22.670
Brother...

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:59.200
East Berlin 
Palace of the Republic

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.370
My comrades, the time has come to unite!

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:05.200
The blame for our failure to end this long war

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.210
lies entirely with the present government.

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:14.710
I know all too well how 
the military police's youth,

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:19.420
who supported the violent measure 
of a coup d'état, must feel!

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.330
They are not rioters,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.290
but youth who burn with idealism.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.810
True patriots!

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.930
But because our country is a democracy,

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:35.810
a change of leadership through 
violence cannot be allowed.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:41.240
For the Republic's safety, I, Erich Schmidt,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:46.740
have been named by the parliament as 
head of the party and minister of state.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:50.750
This is an important assignment, 
without precedent in East German history.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.830
But I shall accept this burden.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:04:00.270
Because it is my calling as a patriot!

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.010
I promise to gather all our military 
forces under the Stasi,

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.390
and form an ever more 
powerful peacekeeping system.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:14.440
In the name of the party, let us become 
sword and shield, and win this war!

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:18.900
My comrades in the USSR have agreed 
to send troops immediately.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.660
I strongly beseech the West to fight 
humanity's enemies with us!

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.430
Comrades!

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:34.580
To keep our homeland from being swallowed 
by the darkness of destruction again,

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.250
so that mothers will not be forced 
to suffer the deaths of their sons,

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.340
let us bring back a stronger Fatherland!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.220
For the Fatherland!

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.140
For the Fatherland!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:51.120
Federal Republic of Germany 
Kiel Base

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.640
The Moscow faction sacrificed the 
Berlin faction to gain control.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.560
It's all a terrible farce.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:58.480
And their defensive lines may 
crumble at any moment.

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.850
They're using their own citizens as hostages.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.610
The West German government will come under 
a lot of criticism if we let Berlin fall.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:11.240
And if we don't like it, we must recognize 
their government and help them?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.750
Worried about them?

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.540
They are my comrades-in-arms.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.260
German Democratic Republic 
Wittstock Training Grounds

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.260
Now is the time to rise.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:28.010
The situation in Berlin is unstable.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.100
If we attack now, we can win!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.180
If we act, so will the other units.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.810
It's too reckless.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.280
The Moscow faction destroyed the 
Berlin faction in short order.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.530
They must have some force we are unaware of.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:47.570
Yes.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:51.120
I succeeded in capturing 
our top priority objective.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:56.620
Now the anti-government factions won't 
be able to rely on the 666th's fame.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:02.960
I'm sure the parliament knows what 
will happen if they oppose us now.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.540
All according to plan.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:06.920
Splendid.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:11.930
That is why you are my successor, 
Major Beatrix Brehme.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.360
I am honored, Comrade Major General...

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.940
No, ruler of East Germany.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.430
Everything is for the Stasi.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:30.160
Lieutenant Lise Hohenstein, 
returning to TSF Werewolf Battalion.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.360
Well done on your special mission.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.950
But...

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.120
Oh, that?

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:40.500
Don't you worry about the two that escaped.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:46.160
Instead, I'd like you to interrogate the 666th.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:51.400
You know them well, so it should 
be easy for you, right?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:53.850
Roger.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.270
Outskirts of Berlin 
Near the Havel River

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.270
Target sighted.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.760
The two pilots have left their unit and escaped.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:08.110
Continuing the search.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:19.960
I see the twins are as perky as ever, Irisdina.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:21.370
Want some?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.940
It's your favorite, himbeertorte.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.800
What are you doing?

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:35.760
I'd always wondered how you made contact 
with the anti-government faction.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:40.010
I never thought Major Hannibal was helping you.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:44.190
It's true that he and they...

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.000
What are you trying to do?

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.690
Torture me to reveal their hideout's location?

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.200
You're going to rot here.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.190
What?

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.410
I'm going to make their ideals a reality.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:06.150
You can just sit and watch, 
unable to do anything.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:12.260
Federal Republic of Germany 
Fort Seelow

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:17.760
BETA echelons 13 and 14 approaching 
from the north and south.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.180
Over one hundred thousand and rising.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.560
Two hours until they reach 
the absolute defense line.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.740
Where's our rear support?

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.060
At this rate...

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.190
You're splitting the division?

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.810
The new government has decided to send

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:40.280
the entire Western Theatre Army, 
as well as the Stasi, to the front lines.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:42.910
You are to split your division in two,

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.520
and deal with the BETAs coming 
from the north and south.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.920
Finish your reorganization today, 
and head to the front lines.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.730
That is all.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:56.910
Major General...

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.250
I'll ask you again.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.190
Tell me who Katia really is.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.820
We know she isn't just an asylum seeker.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:16.870
Stop it, Lise.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.830
If you stop now, you can still turn back.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.830
Were you listening to me?

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.840
You haven't given up your heart entirely.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:37.090
That's why you didn't kill Captain Bernhard.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.970
Am I wrong?

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.310
Don't get cocky.

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.480
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:51.820
Make her wish she'd never been born.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.890
R-Roger!

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.880
Brother...

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:19.430
I'll bring you back, no matter what, okay?

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:35.800
We can't start a fire,

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:39.360
but I'll go see if there's any food.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.180
The hero who saved the nation, 
Lieutenant General Strachwitz.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:06.390
He succeeded in saving officers and troops 
in the retreat from the Ukraine.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:12.420
He may be capable of stopping the BETA 
advance and saving East Germany.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:16.710
Father!

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.080
Theodor!

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:32.830
Wait!

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.710
Get down!

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.690
Stand up, you two.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:52.560
We're getting out of here now.

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:56.360
Comrade Lieutenant Jeckeln!

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.860
Three Days Ago 
East Berlin, Friedrichstrasse

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.720
A MiG-27 Aligatori...

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.550
The latest Soviet TSF?

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:28.170
The Stasi's Moscow faction has stuff like that?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:29.960
You, there.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:35.650
You're Lieutenant Gretel Jeckeln, political 
commissar of the 666th Squadron, right?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.580
M-Me?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.070
No, I'm not...

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.940
Are you trying to pass that off as a disguise?

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:48.280
I'm Suzy Dzap, leader of the resistance 
organization Grosser Bär.

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:52.600
Captain Bernhard told me about you.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.330
We're taking her with us.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:59.900
North Berlin 
Rheinsberg

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:04.380
Honestly...

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:08.890
If you could fool the Stasi just by taking off 
your glasses, no one would fear them.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.890
The 666th really are brave.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:15.980
I-I thought it would work...

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.470
I think you were really cute!

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:20.770
Shut up! I was desperate!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.710
B-But you saved us.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.660
Thanks to everyone...

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.880
Everyone, huh?

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:35.030
It's like a bad joke, isn't it?

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:38.110
A political commissar for the 
German Socialist Unity Party

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:40.670
helping the anti-government forces.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:46.890
But I don't intend to care about 
the party's ideals anymore.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:51.130
Tell me what happened while I was gone.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.310
What happened to our squad?

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.310
W-Well...

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.600
So Hohenstein really was a traitor.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.940
If I'd stayed with the squad, 
this wouldn't have happened.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:25.960
I'm the one who couldn't do anything.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:28.290
I abandoned everyone.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:33.030
No, you did a good job to escape 
and report what happened.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.830
That alone is worth something.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.140
Lieutenant...

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:38.600
So what will you do now?

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:43.980
With Captain Bernhard under arrest, 
we can't count on the 666th.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:47.490
How will you fight the Stasi, now that 
they control the government?

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.450
I have a plan.

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:54.740
I'll negotiate with Major General Franz Heim, 
Commander of the Western Theatre forces.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.750
The Stasi must've sent the 
majority of their troops

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:03.380
to the front lines to stop the BETA assault.

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:08.960
We'll use this opportunity to enter East Berlin 
with the Western Theatre forces.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:14.390
We'll also release the 666th Squadron 
that was captured at Bebersee base.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.390
And if we can take back Captain Bernhard...

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:22.400
Then we can unite people to fight the Stasi?

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:25.480
We sacrifice the front lines for a coup d'état...

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:28.740
We're doing the same thing as the Stasi.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.580
I know.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.710
But there's no other way.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:35.660
Let me ask you one thing.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.160
Can we trust that dopey second lieutenant?

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.600
He was supposedly tricked 
by his sister, who's a spy.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:48.180
He's a valuable pilot who downed 
a Heavy Laser-class.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.670
Can you say for certain he won't betray us?

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.190
If that happens, I'll take responsibility.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:01.700
Wittstock Training Grounds

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.690
I understand your plans.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:08.080
I'll get right to the point.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.820
We can't help you.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.120
Why?

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:15.950
The Stasi have endangered all of Europe!

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:20.820
Irisdina Bernhard, commander of 
East Germany's strongest unit,

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:23.050
the 666th TSF Squadron...

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:29.610
By having such a hero join us as a symbol, 
we could bring the people over to our side

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.050
to fight the Stasi, or so we thought.

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:38.970
But Bernhard's been arrested, and the new 
government is stabilizing the situation.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:45.230
If we rise up now, not enough people 
will join us against the Stasi...

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:48.650
Unless we have a stronger symbol.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.900
We have you!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.070
I'm too weak.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.650
I would simply be called a terrorist, 
and that would be the end.

00:16:56.650 --> 00:16:57.660
Then...

00:16:58.400 --> 00:17:00.240
Checkmate.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:04.420
We have no hero. And so, our war is over.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:09.190
The new government is already 
negotiating with the UN forces.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:13.800
In a few days, troops will come from 
the West to East Germany.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.640
The West doesn't want the 
Stasi running things, either!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:25.080
They don't care who's running things, 
as long as we defeat the BETA.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:28.660
Working with the Stasi to fight 
the BETA and protect this nation

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:31.650
is the only chance we have left.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:33.530
That's all.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.660
Major General...

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:47.700
My forces will leave for the 
Oder-Neisse Line in the early morning.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.620
We won't see each other again.

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:03.900
Wait.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:06.350
There's still a chance.

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.850
And what is that, miss?

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:14.870
If you have a hero to replace Captain 
Bernhard, there's hope, isn't there?

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.610
Yeah, that's right.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:27.870
Do you know who Lieutenant 
General Alfred Strachwitz is?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.940
I understand.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:36.300
If a living hero won't work, then a dead one?

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:41.390
He was a hero of East Germany, 
and a friend of mine.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:45.040
But too much time has passed 
to fight for his sake.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.390
It's impossible.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:50.650
No. The last light hasn't disappeared.

00:18:56.810 --> 00:19:00.700
The name "Katia Waldheim" is fake.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:03.960
Ursula...

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.490
Ursula Strachwitz.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:08.330
That's my real name.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:13.170
I am the daughter of Alfred Strachwitz, 
the man you called a friend.

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.840
The daughter of a hero, 
returned from West Germany,

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:23.370
who fought with Captain Bernhard to protect 
East Germany as part of the strongest TSF unit.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:28.100
If we announce this and use 
me as a symbol to rise up,

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.270
couldn't we fight the Stasi?

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:34.610
To create a country that exists not for 
the government, but for the people.

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:38.160
With no Stasi spying, informants, or purges.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.900
We can be a free, righteous country again.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:45.670
Captain Bernhard told me that's 
what my father wanted.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:52.390
This country is in darkness, and it cannot see 
the future it needs to proceed toward.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:59.430
The sole light we have is a heart that 
wants to save and protect someone.

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.380
The last light...

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.330
If the two Germanys work together,

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.650
we'll never lose to the BETA.

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.630
That's what my dad always said.

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.860
If we're scared of the Stasi
and unable to trust anyone,

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.530
we'll never beat the BETA.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:23.860
I'm willing to use my life for my father, 
who let me escape to West Germany,

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.640
and for everyone who saved and protected me.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:32.350
I don't care what happens to me. 
I have a duty to save East Germany.

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:38.760
Theodor, what is your wish?

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:42.190
I...

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:45.440
I...

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:27.550
What's your mother's name?

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:29.790
Ernestine.

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:32.030
My father used to call her "Tine."

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:37.430
Alfred only told that name 
to those he was close to.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:44.340
Come to think of it, your hair and 
eye color are just like hers.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:49.430
My dad said that I got them from my 
mother, so I had to treasure them.

00:22:50.880 --> 00:22:52.970
Can we believe her?

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:57.820
And it's been a long time since anyone's 
heard the name Strachwitz.

00:22:59.750 --> 00:23:00.600
Major General,

00:23:00.930 --> 00:23:07.240
Katia is the daughter of General Strachwitz, 
and she knows both East and West Germany.

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:09.230
She can be a bridge between the two countries.

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:15.380
I'm Alfred's friend, and I believe it.

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:18.310
No one will doubt me, will they?

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:19.120
No, sir!

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:26.460
Okay, Major General, we don't have a lot of time.

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:25.240
Theodor...

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:28.840
